      "narrative": "Mara Venn's brow furrows at your question. She sets her cup down, tilting her head.\n\n\"Before it was *filed*?\" She repeats the word slowly, as if tasting something off. \"I don't follow. The lock wasn't filed. Toran kept it clean\u2014that's all. Oil, a soft cloth, checked the tumblers once a season. Standard maintenance for a city lock.\"\n\nShe glances over at the bar, where Toran Vex is nervously wiping the same spot on the counter with a rag, his ink-stained cuffs catching the lamplight.\n\n\"Toran's been the lockwright on that gate for\u2014what, eight years now? Before him it was some old dwarven woman named Hestra. Retired. Moved south, I think. But she kept records.\" Mara's eyes drift back to you, and there's a flicker of something\u2014not quite suspicion, but *attention*. \"Why do you ask about filing? That's a very specific word.\"\n\nShe's watching you more closely now, her fingers still on the cup. The question hangs in the air, unanswered."
    },
